WEBVTT

00:00.352 --> 00:03.231
- [Voiceover] We have six
x squared, minus 120 x,

00:03.231 --> 00:05.925
plus 600, equals zero.

00:05.925 --> 00:07.782
Like always, pause this video,

00:07.782 --> 00:09.626
and see if you can solve for x,

00:09.626 --> 00:13.378
if you could find the x values
that satisfy this equation.

00:13.378 --> 00:15.777
Alright, let's work through this together.

00:16.967 --> 00:20.227
The numbers here don't seem
like outlandish numbers.

00:20.227 --> 00:22.944
They seem like something that
I might be able to deal with,

00:22.944 --> 00:26.334
and I might be able to factor,
so let's try to do that.

00:26.334 --> 00:28.261
The first thing I like
to do is see if I can get

00:28.261 --> 00:31.210
a coefficient of one, on
the second degree term,

00:31.210 --> 00:32.789
on the x-squared term.

00:32.789 --> 00:34.878
It looks like actually all of these terms

00:34.878 --> 00:36.208
are divisible by six.

00:36.208 --> 00:38.988
So if we divide both sides
of this equation by six,

00:38.988 --> 00:42.355
I'm still going to have
nice integer coefficients.

00:42.355 --> 00:43.237
Let's do that.

00:43.237 --> 00:45.304
Let's divide both sides by six.

00:45.304 --> 00:48.160
If we divide the left side
by six, divide by six,

00:48.160 --> 00:50.667
divide by six, divide by six.

00:50.667 --> 00:53.407
And I divide the right side by six.

00:53.407 --> 00:55.938
If I do that, and clearly
if I do the same thing

00:55.938 --> 00:57.092
to both sides of the equation,

00:57.092 --> 00:58.864
then the equality still holds.

00:58.864 --> 01:03.755
On the left-hand side, I am
going to be left with x squared,

01:04.970 --> 01:08.499
and then negative 120, divided by six.

01:08.499 --> 01:09.411
That is, let's see.

01:09.411 --> 01:12.071
120 divided by six is 20.

01:12.071 --> 01:15.813
So that's minus 20 x.

01:15.813 --> 01:18.625
Then 600 divided by six, is 100.

01:19.505 --> 01:23.580
So plus 100, is equal
to zero divided by six.

01:23.580 --> 01:25.728
Is equal to zero.

01:25.728 --> 01:27.443
So let's see if we can factor,

01:27.443 --> 01:30.276
if we can express this quadratic

01:30.276 --> 01:32.992
as a product of two expressions.

01:32.992 --> 01:34.385
The way we think about this,

01:34.385 --> 01:36.104
and we've done it multiple times,

01:36.104 --> 01:40.631
if we have something, if we have x plus a,

01:40.631 --> 01:44.254
times x plus b, and this is
hopefully review for you.

01:44.254 --> 01:47.365
If you multiply that out,
that is going to be equal to,

01:47.365 --> 01:52.365
that equals to x squared, plus a, plus b,

01:52.729 --> 01:55.614
x, plus a b.

01:55.614 --> 01:58.772
What we want to do is
see if we can factor this

01:58.772 --> 02:01.396
into an x plus a, and an x plus b.

02:02.416 --> 02:06.007
A plus b, needs to be
equal to negative 20.

02:06.007 --> 02:07.928
That needs to be a plus b.

02:07.928 --> 02:10.969
And then a times b, right over here,

02:10.969 --> 02:12.780
that needs to be equal
to the constant term.

02:12.780 --> 02:15.659
That needs to be a times
b, right over there.

02:15.659 --> 02:19.467
Can we think of two numbers,
that if we take their product,

02:19.467 --> 02:22.927
we get positive 100, and
if we take their sum,

02:22.927 --> 02:24.924
we get negative 20?

02:24.924 --> 02:26.642
Well since their product is positive,

02:26.642 --> 02:29.255
we know that they have the same sign.

02:29.255 --> 02:32.445
They're both going to have the same sign.

02:32.445 --> 02:34.511
They're either both going to be positive,

02:34.511 --> 02:36.090
or their both going to be negative,

02:36.090 --> 02:39.016
since we know that we
have a positive product.

02:39.016 --> 02:41.036
Since their sum is negative,

02:41.036 --> 02:43.567
well they both must both be negative.

02:43.567 --> 02:46.516
You can't add up two positive
numbers, and get a negative.

02:46.516 --> 02:49.859
So they both must be negative.

02:49.859 --> 02:51.345
Let's think about it a little bit.

02:51.345 --> 02:55.566
What negative numbers,
when I add them together

02:55.566 --> 02:59.115
I get negative 20, when
I multiply it, I get 100?

02:59.115 --> 03:00.753
Well you could try to factor 100.

03:00.753 --> 03:03.271
You could say, well negative
two times negative 50,

03:03.271 --> 03:06.475
or negative four times negative 25.

03:06.475 --> 03:07.892
But the one that might jump out at you

03:07.892 --> 03:12.118
is this is negative 10,
times, I'll write it this way,

03:12.118 --> 03:15.229
negative 10, times negative 10,

03:15.229 --> 03:19.339
and this is negative 10, plus negative 10.

03:19.339 --> 03:22.539
So in that case, both our a and
our b, would be negative 10.

03:22.539 --> 03:26.381
And so we can rewrite the
left side of this equation as,

03:26.381 --> 03:29.028
we can rewrite it as,

03:29.028 --> 03:31.234
x, and I'll write it this way at first,

03:31.234 --> 03:33.853
x plus negative 10,

03:35.181 --> 03:36.636
times,

03:39.206 --> 03:42.204
x plus negative 10 again.

03:42.204 --> 03:44.412
X plus negative 10,

03:45.527 --> 03:48.470
and that is going to be equal to zero.

03:48.470 --> 03:50.722
So all I've done is I've
factored this quadratic.

03:50.722 --> 03:54.205
Another way, these are both
the same thing as x minus 10.

03:54.205 --> 03:59.205
I could rewrite this
as x minus 10, squared,

03:59.662 --> 04:02.010
is equal to zero.

04:03.066 --> 04:04.840
The only way that the left-hand side

04:04.840 --> 04:06.186
is going to be equal to zero,

04:06.186 --> 04:08.230
is if x minus 10 is equal to zero.

04:08.230 --> 04:09.274
You could think of this as taking

04:09.274 --> 04:11.759
the square root of both sides.

04:11.759 --> 04:12.943
It doesn't matter if
you're taking the positive

04:12.943 --> 04:14.738
or negative square root, or both of them.

04:14.738 --> 04:16.588
The square root of zero, is zero.

04:16.588 --> 04:21.588
So, we would say, that x minus
10 needs to be equal to zero.

04:21.650 --> 04:24.785
So x , adding 10 to both sides of this,

04:24.785 --> 04:28.796
you have x is equal to 10, is the solution

04:28.796 --> 04:32.117
to this quadratic equation, up here.
